  <prompt>
    Write the PDF-intake seam test that proves the END-TO-END flow: a PDF NDA OPENS in Compose (via the 040 PDF →
    canonical model intake), is EDITED, and SAVES as a docx version through render-on-save (no 422, new SPE version) —
    Success Criterion 2. Also assert the lossiness-expectation UX (honest fixed-layout / lossier-than-docx / version-
    history-is-the-safety-net message) is present. Use an ADR-038 seam / KEEP-path vertical slice over the REAL intake
    path — NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration test, NO ctor-null test.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer writing an end-to-end integration/seam test spanning PDF intake (040) + client wiring (041). Expert in ADR-038's KEEP-path seam model (real components, no `Mock&lt;...&gt;`, no DI/ctor tests) and in asserting a render-on-save docx-version outcome. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    An end-to-end seam test at the `tests/integration/seam/Compose/**` KEEP path: a PDF NDA fixture projects into the
    canonical model (040), opens/edits through the client path (041), and saves as a docx version via render-on-save
    (no 422, new version) — plus an assertion that the honest-lossiness UX message is surfaced. Fails loudly if intake
    hard-fails, if save does not produce a docx version, or if the lossiness message is absent.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Success Criterion 2: "A PDF NDA opens in Compose, is edited, and saves as a docx version — verify by an end-to-end
      run on a PDF NDA." Task 040 built the intake, 041 wired the client. This task is the standing regression net for
      the full PDF round-trip and the honest-lossiness UX. Because it exercises the real intake path with no mocks, it is
      an ADR-038 seam vertical slice. Use a PDF NDA fixture (the corpus NDA or a PDF rendition) so the test mirrors the
      real worst-offender.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ — the end-to-end PDF-intake seam test (PDF NDA opens → edit → save-as-docx-version; lossiness UX asserted).</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/DocumentIntelligenceService.cs — the 040 PDF → canonical model intake under test (real component, no mocks).</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx — the 041 open→edit→save-as-docx + lossiness UX under test.</file>
      <file role="reference">tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/ — the NDA fixture (or a PDF rendition) to drive the end-to-end test.</file>
      <file role="adr">docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md — seam / KEEP-path vertical slice; banned mock/DI/ctor tests.</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/spec.md — FR-06, Success Criterion 2, honest-lossiness UX.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="041" status="pending">Client open→edit→save-as-docx wiring + lossiness UX — the flow this end-to-end test asserts against.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / Success Criterion 2">The test MUST prove the end-to-end PDF NDA flow: opens (via 040 intake) → edited → saves as a docx version via render-on-save (no 422, new SPE version). Scope: use a PDF NDA fixture; the intake is 040's, the save is the R6 render-on-save path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / honest-lossiness">The test MUST assert the honest-lossiness UX message is surfaced on PDF open (fixed-layout / lossier than docx / version history is the safety net). Scope: presence + honesty (no "identical to source" claim).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">The test is a seam / KEEP-path vertical slice over the REAL intake path. Scope: NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration test, NO ctor-null test — drive the actual components end-to-end at `tests/integration/seam/Compose/**`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / ADR-013">The test exercises the pure intake + Compose path (`byte[]`/OOXML in, projection out; `PublicContracts/` seams). Scope: no `Microsoft.Graph`, no AI-internal type, no `Services/Ai/` fork in the test path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / BFF Hygiene §10">No runtime package added. Scope: `dotnet publish -c Release` unaffected — report size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expect ~0); `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

