        Drive a PDF NDA fixture through the real 040 intake → canonical model → 041 open/edit → render-on-save; assert a docx version is produced (no 422) and the lossiness message is surfaced. No mocks — real components end-to-end.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor declaration: 🔒 RIGOR LEVEL: STANDARD (plan.md §5) / 📋 REASON: test-modifying `tests/**` → TEST-MODIFYING override (root §8) makes Step 9.5 gates UNCONDITIONAL / 📖 PROTOCOL STEPS. Load Success Criterion 2, FR-06, ADR-038.</step>
    <step order="1" name="RE-GREP the seam path + fixture">Confirm the established `tests/integration/seam/Compose/**` path and the PDF NDA fixture (or a PDF rendition) to drive the end-to-end test.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Write the end-to-end seam test">Drive the PDF NDA through the real 040 intake → 041 open/edit → render-on-save; assert a docx version is produced (no 422) and the honest-lossiness message is surfaced. No banned mock/DI/ctor tests.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Build + hygiene">`dotnet test` (+ client test if applicable) green; `dotnet publish -c Release` size + delta (0). `/conflict-check` before the PR.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Close out">Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set task 042 to ✅. Record any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the PDF NDA intake hard-fails (422), if save does not produce a docx version, or if the lossiness message is absent — STOP. Do NOT weaken the assertions to make the test pass; surface which stage failed (intake / save / UX) so 040 or 041 is fixed. A green test that hides a hard-fail or a false "identical to source" claim would falsely satisfy Success Criterion 2.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run the seam test suite; `dotnet publish -c Release` for the size check.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Run the Compose client test if the end-to-end assertion spans the client.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ — end-to-end PDF-intake seam test (PDF NDA opens → edit → save-as-docx-version; lossiness UX asserted)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a PDF NDA fixture, when driven through the real 040 intake → 041 open/edit → render-on-save, then a docx version is produced with no 422 and a new SPE version.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test asserts the honest-lossiness UX message is surfaced on PDF open (fixed-layout / lossier than docx / version history is the safety net) with no "identical to source" claim.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test is an ADR-038 seam / KEEP-path slice over the real intake path — no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration test, no ctor-null test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if intake hard-fails, save yields no docx version, or the lossiness message is absent, the test FAILS loudly (and the escalation fires) — the assertions are not weakened.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet test` seam suite green; publish size ~0 MB delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline; `/conflict-check` clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">TASK-INDEX.md shows task 042 as ✅ and any deviation is recorded in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

